@startuml
autoactivate on
autonumber

actor "User" as User
participant ":System" as System
participant "Google Cloud\nVision" as Vision
participant "Spotify" as Spotify

activate User

User -> System: asks to scan an album cover
opt camera permission not yet granted
  System --> User: requests camera permission
  User -> System: grants or denies permission
end
alt permission denied
  System --> User: informs that camera permission is denied
else permission granted
  System --> User: opens the camera
  User -> System: takes a photo of the cover
  alt photo cancelled or unreadable
    System --> User: returns to the main menu
  else photo ok
    System -> Vision: sends the photo for text and web detection
    Vision --> System: returns the text on the cover, the best guess,\nthe matching pages and the matching images
    alt no usable text and no Spotify link
      System --> User: informs that nothing could be read or recognised
    else clues found
      System -> Spotify: gets the albums whose Spotify link appeared next to the cover
      Spotify --> System: returns the albums
      System -> Spotify: searches albums with each clue, most reliable first (at most 5 searches)
      Spotify --> System: returns up to 10 albums per search
      alt no albums found
        System --> User: informs that the album was not found
      else
        System --> User: shows the list of candidate albums (at most 10; just one when an album\nhas the same cover image or clearly matches the clues)
        User -> System: chooses an album
        System --> User: shows the album details
      end
    end
  end
end

note right of System
  Network or API failures show an error
  message and return to the previous screen.
  The back button cancels the analysis at any time.
end note
@enduml
